  "reason": "Evidence: The current best configuration (config_005: RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieves 0.650 acc, showing that (a) multiprofile + avgpool is a strong combination and (b) scvi_n200 outperforms PCA_n2000 by ~0.059 under identical settings. However, we have no data on scgpt, a third learned encoder, and it is unclear whether it can match or exceed scvi_n200. Question tested: config_008 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) holds profile setting and aggregation constant while swapping the encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt, cleanly isolating the encoder effect. Why best next: Under a limited budget, establishing which RNA encoder is superior before committing to multimodal experiments (which are more complex and expensive) is the highest-information-value step. A clean A/B encoder comparison under the best-known profile/aggregation settings will either reveal a new best encoder to exploit in subsequent multimodal trials or confirm scvi_n200 as the optimal backbone, reducing uncertainty about the most impactful design axis before we add fusion complexity."
